# Run Checklist

## Purpose

This checklist is the operator-facing progress tracker for the run. It is created by KHS/Hermes during the `plan` phase, after KAB `plan read` has produced `plan.plan_text`, and is updated after `ask` and every later phase. Do not treat it as optional notes.

KAB does not own this file. KAB supplies the backend-authored plan text and source evidence. KHS should ask KAB's planner backend to include a parse-friendly `KHS Checklist Seed` in `plan.plan_text`; KHS/Hermes then converts that seed plus the KHS phase contract into this normalized progress checklist and stores it as a KAH artifact.

## Checklist Rules

- Every canonical KHS phase must have a row.
- Required phases must not be removed.
- Skipped or not-applicable phases must keep a row with an explicit reason.
- Simple reports/status checks, investigations/research evidence, and docs-only tasks must not inherit implementation, enhance-test, optimize, or broad review loops unless the task contract records a classification change.
- Each row must name the expected artifact or evidence used to prove completion.
- Backend console summaries must stay English and compact: Status, Summary, Files, Verification, Risks/blockers, Detailed artifact, Next action requested.
- Detailed backend output must be artifact-first under `.kkachi/runs/<run_id>/artifacts/<phase>/backend-<phase>.md`; artifact-write blockers fail closed instead of triggering full chat dumps.
- When compact continuity artifacts are present, use read-summary-first retrieval: read `run-summary.yaml` first, then the relevant `phase-packets/<phase>.yaml`, then targeted source artifact ranges only when a decision requires exact evidence.
- Phase packets and run summaries must preserve source artifact paths and checksums; they never authorize evidence discard, Hermes proxy/headroom/runtime context-pruning requirements, KAH subjective summarization, KAB compression-policy decisions, or auth/token/provider/gateway/model mutation.
- Code-change and process-changing runs must include CodeGraph refresh evidence before backend planning.
- Code-change runs must record the selected verification profile/gate evidence after implementation, test enhancement, AI slop cleanup, and optimization whenever those stages change files. Do not assume `make test`; use the selected profile/gate id, command, timeout, applicability, status, exit code, duration, log path, log checksum, bounded failure excerpt, and deterministic failure extractor posture.
- Hermes updates `State` after each phase and uses this file during `final_verify`.

## State Values

- `pending`
- `in_progress`
- `done`
- `skipped`
- `blocked`

