## Final Checklist Review

- [ ] Every required phase is `done`.
- [ ] Every skipped phase has a reason.
- [ ] Every conditional phase has an applicability decision.
- [ ] Every completed phase links to evidence.
- [ ] CodeGraph refresh evidence exists for code/process-changing tasks, or an explicit unavailable/degraded reason is recorded.
- [ ] Feedback rounds are between 1 and 5.
- [ ] Code-change runs include implementation/test-enhancement/slop-cleanup/optimization evidence for the selected verification profile/gate after the last relevant change, or explicit `not_applicable` reasons.
- [ ] Roadmap completion was marked only after implementation, verification, KAH evidence, and required reviews supported completion.
- [ ] Final verification checked KAH gates and KAB evidence when the run is KAB-backed or claims backend runtime evidence.
- [ ] Compact phase packets and run summary, when present, are current and preserve artifact paths, checksums, retrieval instructions, invalidation behavior, and compression-forbidden direct references.
